This is where level 30 may hurt you. You have no more slots to advance. As a
spellcaster you need to pay attention to the spells you'll actually use,
their level, and the slots associated with it. For example a high level wizard
probably isn't going to cast any clerical spells. Here's the list:

clerical          : Level
  protection      :   1
  create monster  :   2
  remove curse    :   3
  create familiar :   6
  turn undead     :   6

Now consider: prot is a waste. Create monster is in a wand. Remove curse is
in a scroll you can write. Charm monster (enchantment) can give you a pet
whenever you like, and not only is turn undead in a wand, you'll probably
just beat on any undead anyway. 

So why then do you need ANY? clerical slots.

Same with healing. Full healing potions and a blessed unicorn horn will give 
you every advantage You can get from a spell. Downgrade your slots.

As you approach endgame you'll actually want the two top level matter spells:
(polymorph at level 6 and cacellation at level 7). Bump those up.

So now you actually have to get your level dropped. Imagine that!

Two ways to do it. Get naked and dance with a wraith. The other is to piss your
god off by praying before the prayer timeout and keep praying. 

Getting back to your god's good graces can be tough. But be aware that you 
shouldn't pray in Gehennom under any circumstances anyway. So you probably
can afford to piss of the god dude(tte) drop a few levels. Regain them and
reassign the slots. But pissing off one's god is dangerous business as
you can get lightning and disintegration beams thrown at you from above!

Another tactic is to simply gear up with the robe and maxed out helm of 
brilliance. Along with your level, it should offset any negatives. It's
probably your best bet.

